Z||000053||GarethWright||09-29-2001||02:15 PM||||<B><BR>9/28/01 <P>Important Announcements.Thank you all for the overwhelming response to the Motor City Online Beta Test!<P>We've met and exceeded our anticipated numbers by hundreds-- even thousands-- of players. The testing continues, however many people are unable to play due to the great number of people trying to access our servers. This is exciting for the development team, but not a good experience for our players. To fix this problem, we're doing two things:<P>1) On Tuesday, after testing a fix for the overload problems found so far on our first server set, we'll be bringing up a second, brand-new server set online to allow more new players to log in and play.<P>2) As we have almost an overabundance of people wishing to test our Beta at this time, the downloadable version of the Motor City Online Beta currently located on FilePlanet will be discontinued starting at midnight Pacific Time on Monday, 10/1.<P>Thanks again for your support, and we hope to see you very soon in the live version of Motor City Online!<P>~~The Motor City Online Development Team<BR></B><P>If anyone wants to play for free, now is the time to download, from Fileplanet at least, though I would recommend using the link posted by loafer87gt, as it didnt have a wait time to download.  Its 483mb and takes 24 hours at 56k.<BR>||||reg||1
